 ## Background
-Hierarchical traversal originated with the development of ray tracing acceleration structures. Kay and Kajiya (1986) introduced a hierarchy traversal algorithm for ray-object intersection, demonstrating significant speedups [S5, unofficial]. In volume rendering, the concept was adapted to Octrees and Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVOs) to handle large, sparse datasets efficiently [S1, unofficial]. The technique is used for volume rendering octrees or kd-trees, similar to tree traversal in ray tracing [S6, unofficial].
